WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
Dr. Chaos, do you dare open the doors to doom?

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:27.060
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.180
I'm Mike. And I'm Sean.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.320
And again, that is it.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:32.900
We have been abandoned.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.200
And we're abandoned in a haunted castle this time.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:37.260
Is it a castle?

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.280
Looks like a house. Can it really be described as a castle?

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.540
Yeah, exactly. I mean, I guess a house is a man's castle.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.100
We have a lot of house cleaning here to do right at the top, Sean.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.340
How so? Well, did you just say house so?

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.800
Was you making a very clever house pun?

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:56.860
I didn't mean to.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:58.380
That's very funny.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.020
Well, you know, first off, what a title.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:02.460
Dr. Chaos.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:04.260
Yeah. What are you what are you expecting?

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.060
Well, we were just having a conversation.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:13.060
We were having a conversation. Me, you and one other person that shall not be named at this moment.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:22.760
And he can he said that it was like a prog metal album, which I thought was I thought was actually pretty apt.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:27.760
What I what I was expecting was probably just another bland 3D.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:37.120
I'm sorry. Another bland side scrolling platformer of, you know, maybe it's going to have some spooky like vampires or something.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:42.760
I don't know. And you weren't expecting this game to be like an autobiography of Joseph Kanopka.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.840
Could you could you elaborate on that?

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:50.000
Joseph Kanopka, also known as Dr.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:58.060
Chaos, was an American citizen who served 16 years of a 20 year prison sentence for two felony acts of conspiracy to commit acts of terror.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:05.560
So, OK, this is part of, you know, of this is a blind spot of mine, I guess.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:08.380
What were these acts of terror he was going to commit?

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:09.860
Well, they were only conspiracy.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:19.880
So we you know, we can't I don't want to pin the guy down and say that he was definitely going to do these things because technically he didn't get a chance to go through with them.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.740
But he is Dr.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:25.060
Chaos. That's how he was referred to.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.020
And if you try to look up Dr.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.740
Chaos, you won't get the NES game.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:33.860
I guarantee it. I guarantee even if you like only search for NES games, you're going to get this guy first.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.740
Oh, my God. All right.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.140
Yeah. I'm looking at the Wikipedia page now.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.040
Yeah, he definitely looks like he might.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.400
I think it's the sunglasses.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:47.280
Yeah. He looks more like an agent of chaos than a Dr.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:52.760
Chaos. I wonder what his I wonder what his big plan was.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:54.840
Well, enough about him.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.740
And let's talk about Dr.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:02.660
Jin Chaos, who is the mad physicist that the game is named after.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:07.940
What were your I don't even want to ask, like, what were your impressions of this guy?

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.460
I don't think we ever really see him.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.580
But I don't Dr.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.160
Jin Chaos is a pretty cool name.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:20.160
And I will say that looking through the manual, this is one of the more coherent and cogent backstories.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.260
So much so that it actually like it.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.700
It does make sense when you're playing the game that this is sort of what's happening.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.560
It's not a good story.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.460
And it has plot holes even in like the summary.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:48.820
I don't know why in the letter that he leaves, he says that you, your brother of of just a generic background of the only one that can save the house and the world.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.280
But, you know, we're getting there.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.680
It's not a bunch of word salads now.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.940
Yeah, it's kind of fun until they just named the other character Michael.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.680
Like, you mean, Dr.

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:04.140
Jin Chaos's brother is just Michael Chaos?

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:13.480
Wow. I mean, is this just because like, do you feel like you have like a complex about your name, Mike?

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:22.160
Well, first off, I will say that they were probably making some reference to the archangel Michael, who, you know, defeated Satan.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.740
Who's actually named after you.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.320
Right. Everybody knows that part, too.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:31.080
Yeah. You know, just the interesting thing here, I guess, is that why go through all the trouble?

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:36.760
Like Dr. Jin Chaos feels like that was left over from the Japanese side of the game.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.940
And then they forgot to translate that.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:43.400
And instead they just translated the brother's name to Michael because that's very English facing.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:50.480
I mean, I guess what I would say and Jin sounds like a pretty English name and chaos is an English word.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:05:03.500
But I guess what you could do to, you know, headcanon this is to just say that it's like a very like, I don't know, like a Slavic name, like Chopped Chouse or something like that.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:04.840
I guess I'm just a little.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:06.480
Yeah, sure.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:07.580
That sounds great, too.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:08.620
Chouse. I like that.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:13.180
Or, you know, the Sonic Adventure Chouse, the Chow Garden.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:14.400
Yeah. Are you familiar with that?

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:15.800
Yeah. I had Chouse.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:22.060
Because they're technically chaos because of the chaos emeralds in Sonic, but we call them Chouse instead.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:31.220
Yeah. I think that I actually never heard the word Chow in like an official capacity.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.800
It was just. I'm making it official right now, right here.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:35.020
I'm taking my stand.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:36.580
Come after me, Sonic fans.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.440
Yeah. There are dozens of you.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:40.900
I will stand beside you.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.000
And we have, you know, Dr.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:49.720
Jin Chaos, who's invented an interdimensional warp gate, which grants access to other worlds.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:54.620
But unfortunately, that portal invites a world of monsters into the castle.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:06:02.620
Michael. His younger brother, just a regular guy named Michael, shows up just in time to notice that his brother, Dr.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:04.320
Chaos, is missing.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:06.840
And then he goes and tries to fix everything.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:08.960
And that's what you do in the game.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:10.100
Because you are Michael.

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:11.940
You are Michael.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:16.680
You don't think they picked Michael because of like Michael Jackson or Michael Jordan?

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:22.880
Like. I think he's supposed to be an everyman and nobody of note has ever really been named Michael.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:24.960
Understood. Okay.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:30.860
Yep. I think there's like a council of Michaels who would like to differ with you there.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:33.400
So, Dr.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:36.280
Chaos, you start, you're Michael, you start right outside the house.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:40.300
I think it's cute that they let you start outside the house because you can't walk around outside.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:44.100
It's just jump up the first step, which is something everybody does, right?

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:45.820
You can't just walk up your steps.

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:47.100
You got to jump up over that.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:49.240
Yeah. It's for the immersion. Yeah, I get it.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:52.880
And you might hit your head on the doorframe after the jump.

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:59.300
So, they very literally coded that in there, too.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:06.060
Great. And then you walk in through the door and, you know, I hear monsters came through an interdimensional

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:10.020
portal and I think like, all right, that sounds like we're going to see some pretty scary stuff.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:12.120
And then it's just like mice and bats.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:17.140
Okay. Well, that's just like what happened to the house while it's been without a caretaker.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:18.840
You know, like the door was wide open.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:23.500
When you go on vacation, your house just has mice and bats when you come back?

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:26.780
If I left the door open like his brother was, yeah.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:29.240
All right. No, I can deal with that.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:33.320
I mean, in Animal Crossing, if you don't visit your house for a while, there's like cockroaches

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:34.580
inside. Yeah.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.720
Yeah, I mean, this is just the things that happen.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:08:06.260
With 

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:24.660
Let's just rewind for a second

